            [[['bk-diff add:+', ' c', ' · ', 'bk-diff gone:−', ' a'], ['setup.list_order']], [['bk-diff add:+', ' y', ' · ', 'bk-diff gone:−', ' x'], ['–']], ['−', 'setup.mark_gone']],
            [$r['list'] ?? null, $r['known'] ?? null, $r['mark'] ?? null]);
        $bjs2 = (string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_WEB . '/desks/backup/desk.js');
        check('apply dialog marks: a gone app «−», every new thing on the server «+», a value «old → new» without a mark',
            str_contains($bjs2, "li.append(diffMark('gone'), T('setup.ch_app_gone'") && str_contains($bjs2, "li.append(diffMark('add'), name);")
            && str_contains($bjs2, ": `\${valueText(saved[k], k)} → \${valueText(view[k], k)}`"));
        foreach (['en', 'de', 'it', 'fr', 'es'] as $l) {
            $bk = json_decode((string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_WEB . "/desks/backup/lang/$l.json"), true) ?: [];
            same("apply dialog marks: $l — the marks' words and the partnership rows", [], array_values(array_filter(['setup.mark_add', 'setup.mark_gone', 'partner.ch_gone',
                'partner.ch_new', 'partner.ch_changed', 'partner.apply_new', 'partner.apply_from'], fn ($k) => !isset($bk[$k]))));
        }
    }
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp));
}

/**
 * 1.64 (USOPartner, 2026-10-15): Mr. Backupsy not hired there, a settings.ini left from before still sends pdata and the
 * place to an ended pair «USO-Test-Server» (the same server, since paired anew and renamed «Tower») — the Team Lead said
 * «units of USO-Test-Server wait … apply». The Apply hint only with Mr. Backupsy hired, naming this pair; the pair's name
 * follows what the partner calls itself (the watch, and the step partner-names for a pairs.json already stale).
 */
function testPartnerStaleName(): void
{
    if (posix_geteuid() !== 0) {
        check('partner stale name: root only — not run here', true);
        return;
    }
    $tmp = hardeningTmp('partner-stale-name');
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp) . '/*');
    $A = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/A");
    @mkdir("$A[data]/partner", 0700, true);
    @mkdir("$A[data]/office", 0755, true);
    $hk = ['SHA256:' . str_repeat('q', 43)];
    $tower = partnerTestPair('c3553dcc', ['name' => 'Tower', 'address' => '192.168.7.111', 'host_keys' => $hk]);
    $priv = function (string $f, array $j): void {
        file_put_contents($f, json_encode($j));
        chmod($f, 0600);
    };
    $priv("$A[data]/partner/pairs.json", ['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [$tower]]);
    $priv("$A[data]/partner/ended.json", ['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [
        '26bbb6eb' => ['name' => 'USO-Test-Server', 'address' => '192.168.7.111', 'port' => 22, 'host_keys' => $hk, 'time' => time() - 100]]]);
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/unraid-backup/settings.ini", "[general]\npartner_place = 26bbb6eb\n[partner \"26bbb6eb\"]\nname = USO-Test-Server\naddress = 192.168.7.111\nport = 22\n"
        . "[share \"pdata\"]\nmode = snapshot\npartner = 26bbb6eb\n");
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/office/staff.json", json_encode(['hired' => ['advisor' => 1, 'restore' => 1]]));
    $card = fn () => partnerTestAs($A, 'return partnerPublic();');
    $c = $card();
    same('partner stale name: USOPartner\'s state — Mr. Backupsy not hired: no «apply» hint on the card, the need line asks to hire him',
        [[], false, 'Tower'], [$c['pairs'][0]['apply_from'] ?? 'missing', $c['ready']['backup_hired'] ?? null, $c['pairs'][0]['name'] ?? null]);
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/office/staff.json", json_encode(['hired' => ['advisor' => 1, 'restore' => 1, 'backup' => 1]]));
    $c = $card();
    same('partner stale name: … Mr. Backupsy hired: the 2 units wait for this pair', 2, array_sum(array_column($c['pairs'][0]['apply_from'] ?? [], 'n')));
    $js = (string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_WEB . '/desks/caretaker/partner.js');
    check('partner stale name: the card names this pair (x.name), never the ended pair\'s old name, and says nothing of the setup without Mr. Backupsy',
        str_contains($js, "T('partner.i_send_apply', { name: x.name,") && str_contains($js, "else if (!hired) send.append(T('partner.i_send_not_yet'));") && !str_contains($js, 'from.map((f) => f.name)'));
    foreach (['en', 'de', 'it', 'fr', 'es'] as $l) {
        $ct = json_decode((string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_WEB . "/desks/caretaker/lang/$l.json"), true) ?: [];
        check("partner stale name: $l — the apply line names {name}, not {from}; «not sent yet» there",
            str_contains($ct['partner.i_send_apply']['other'] ?? '', '{name}') && !str_contains(json_encode($ct['partner.i_send_apply'] ?? []), '{from}')
            && is_string($ct['partner.i_send_not_yet'] ?? null));
    }

    // the partner renamed on its side: its status says the name — the pair follows (the watch and «Ask now»)
    $ask = ['reachable' => true, 'status' => ['name' => 'Tower2'], 'answer' => ['array' => 'started', 'night' => false, 'v' => '1.64.0'], 'time' => time(), 'why' => null];
    $r = partnerTestAs($A, 'return partnerNameFollow(partnerPair("c3553dcc"), ' . var_export($ask, true) . ')["name"];');
    same('partner stale name: renamed on the other side — pairs.json takes the name its status says', ['Tower2', 'Tower2'],
        [$r, partnerTestAs($A, 'return partnerPair("c3553dcc")["name"];')]);
    same('partner stale name: … an unreachable partner or a bad name changes nothing', ['Tower2', 'Tower2'], [
        partnerTestAs($A, 'return partnerNameFollow(partnerPair("c3553dcc"), ["reachable" => false, "status" => ["name" => "Other"]])["name"];'),
        partnerTestAs($A, 'return partnerNameFollow(partnerPair("c3553dcc"), ["reachable" => true, "status" => ["name" => "bad;name\n"]])["name"];')]);
    $src = (string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_DIR . '/agent/lib/partner.php');
    check('partner stale name: the watch and «Ask now» both follow the name', substr_count($src, 'partnerNameFollow(') === 3);

    // the step partner-names: a pairs.json already stale takes the name state.json's last status said
    $priv("$A[data]/partner/pairs.json", ['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [$tower + [], ['id' => 'f2f2f2f2', 'kind' => 'mirror', 'name' => 'mirrorbox']]]);
    $priv("$A[data]/partner/state.json", ['pairs' => ['c3553dcc' => ['status' => ['name' => 'USOTower']]], 'time' => time()]);
    $mig = fn () => partnerTestAs($A, 'return partnerMigrateNames(' . var_export($A['data'], true) . ');');
    $said = $mig();
    $now = json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$A[data]/partner/pairs.json"), true);
    same('partner stale name: migration — the name taken, the entry it doesn\'t know kept, a copy beside', ['USOTower', 'mirror', true],
        [$now['pairs'][0]['name'] ?? null, $now['pairs'][1]['kind'] ?? null, is_file("$A[data]/partner/pairs.json.before-partner-names")]);
    same('partner stale name: migration again — nothing to change', 'every pair carries its partner\'s name already', $mig());
    same('partner stale name: no pairs.json — nothing to change', 'no pairs.json — nothing to change', partnerMigrateNames("$tmp/nowhere"));
    same('partner stale name: the step is registered for 1.64.0', '1.64.0', array_column(officeMigrateSteps(), 'version', 'id')['partner-names'] ?? null);
}

function testPartnerUnits(): void
{
    if (posix_geteuid() !== 0) {
        check('partner units: root only — not run here', true);
        return;
    }
    $tmp = hardeningTmp('partner-units');
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp) . '/*');
    $v = fn (?array $a, string $k) => is_array($a) && array_key_exists($k, $a) ? $a[$k] : 'missing';      // a key that may hold null

    // ---- the shapes: a pair of up to 1.59 is read as it is (its unit lists and window stripped), written in the shape of 1.60
    $file = "$tmp/p/pairs.json";
    @mkdir("$tmp/p", 0700, true);
    $old = partnerTestPair('a1b2c3d4', ['send' => ['units' => ['share:media'], 'rate_mbit' => 5, 'wanted' => ['share:media', 'place'], 'offered' => 1791400000],
        'receive' => ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'window' => '00:00-07:00', 'wake' => false, 'units' => ['share:appdata']]]);
    file_put_contents($file, json_encode(['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [$old]]));
    chmod($file, 0600);
    $read = partnerPairs($file)[0] ?? [];
    same('units: a pair of up to 1.59 is taken — send only its rate, receive its rules', [['rate_mbit' => 5], ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'wake' => false]],
        [$read['send'] ?? null, $read['receive'] ?? null]);
    check('units: … reading writes nothing', isset(json_decode((string) file_get_contents($file), true)['pairs'][0]['send']['wanted']));
    partnerPairsWrite([$old], $file);
    same('units: … the next write has the shape of 1.60', [['rate_mbit' => 5], ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'wake' => false]],
        [json_decode((string) file_get_contents($file), true)['pairs'][0]['send'] ?? null, json_decode((string) file_get_contents($file), true)['pairs'][0]['receive'] ?? null]);
    $pre229 = partnerTestPair('a1b2c3d4', ['send' => ['units' => ['share:media'], 'rate_mbit' => 7]]);
    file_put_contents($file, json_encode(['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [$pre229]]));
    same('units: a pair of before 2.29 (send without wanted) is taken too', ['rate_mbit' => 7], partnerPairs($file)[0]['send'] ?? null);
    $bad = [
        'send with units of a path' => ['send' => ['units' => ['share:../x'], 'rate_mbit' => 0]],
        'send wanted without units' => ['send' => ['units' => [], 'rate_mbit' => 0, 'offered' => null]],
        'send with an extra key' => ['send' => ['rate_mbit' => 0, 'agreed' => []]],
        'send without a rate' => ['send' => []],
        'a rate as text' => ['send' => ['rate_mbit' => '5']],
        'receive with the window only' => ['receive' => ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'window' => '00:00-07:00', 'wake' => false]],
        'receive with the units only' => ['receive' => ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'wake' => false, 'units' => ['share:appdata']]],
        'receive with an extra key' => ['receive' => ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'wake' => false, 'mode' => 'x']],
        'receive without wake' => ['receive' => ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0']],
    ];
    foreach ($bad as $what => $over) {
        file_put_contents($file, json_encode(['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [$over + partnerTestPair('a1b2c3d4')]]));
        same("units: pairs.json — $what: no pair", [], partnerPairs($file));
    }
    // a partner's status: takes_all (a door since 1.60), agreed (what it received, or an older office's agreement)
    $clean = partnerStatusClean(['ok' => true, 'agreed' => ['place', 'share:appdata'], 'takes_all' => true, 'wish' => [], 'units' => ['share:old' => ['snaps' => ['uso-backup-20261001-0200']]]]);
    same('units: status — takes_all and agreed kept, every unit in shape shown', [true, ['place', 'share:appdata'], ['share:old']], [$clean['takes_all'] ?? null, $clean['agreed'] ?? null, array_keys($clean['units'] ?? [])]);
    same('units: status of an office up to 1.59 — agreed only, no takes_all', [false, ['place']], [$v(partnerStatusClean(['ok' => true, 'agreed' => ['place'], 'wish' => []]), 'takes_all'),
        partnerStatusClean(['ok' => true, 'agreed' => ['place'], 'wish' => []])['agreed'] ?? null]);
    same('units: status of an office before 2.29 — no agreed, no takes_all', [null, false], [$v(partnerStatusClean(['ok' => true]), 'agreed'), $v(partnerStatusClean(['ok' => true]), 'takes_all')]);

    // ---- the migration step partner-simple: a copy, the new shape, the units sent so far for Mr. Backupsy's setup
    $M = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/M");
    @mkdir("$M[data]/partner", 0700, true);
    file_put_contents("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json", json_encode(['v' => 1, 'pairs' => [
        partnerTestPair('a1b2c3d4', ['send' => ['units' => ['share:media'], 'rate_mbit' => 5, 'wanted' => ['share:media', 'place'], 'offered' => null],
            'receive' => ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'window' => '00:00-07:00', 'wake' => false, 'units' => ['share:appdata']]]),
        partnerTestPair('b2c3d4e5', ['their_key' => null, 'receive' => null, 'send' => ['units' => [], 'rate_mbit' => 0]]),
        ['id' => 'f2f2f2f2', 'kind' => 'mirror', 'name' => 'mirrorbox']]]));
    chmod("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json", 0600);
    $mig = fn () => partnerTestAs($M, 'return partnerMigrateSimple(' . var_export($M['data'], true) . ');');
    $said = $mig();
    $now = json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json"), true);
    same('migration: two pairs written in the shape of 1.60, the entry it doesn\'t know kept, a copy beside', [2, ['rate_mbit' => 5], ['pool' => 'tank', 'quota_gb' => 10, 'retention' => '2 0 0', 'wake' => false], ['rate_mbit' => 0], 'mirror', true],
        [count(array_filter($now['pairs'], fn ($p) => isset($p['send']['rate_mbit']) && count($p['send']) === 1)), $now['pairs'][0]['send'] ?? null, $now['pairs'][0]['receive'] ?? null,
         $now['pairs'][1]['send'] ?? null, $now['pairs'][2]['kind'] ?? null, is_file("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json.before-partner-simple")]);
    check('migration: the copy is the file as it was (root only), the log line says what happened', str_contains((string) file_get_contents("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json.before-partner-simple"), '"wanted"')
        && (fileperms("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json.before-partner-simple") & 0777) === 0600 && str_contains($said, '2 pair(s)') && str_contains($said, 'share:media, place'), $said);
    same('migration: migrated.json — the units each pair sent so far (send.units ∪ wanted)', ['a1b2c3d4' => ['share:media', 'place']], json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$M[data]/partner/migrated.json"), true)['pairs'] ?? null);
    $copy = (string) file_get_contents("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json.before-partner-simple");
    same('migration: run again — nothing to change, the copy untouched', ['the pairs are in the shape of 1.60 already', true], [$mig(), file_get_contents("$M[data]/partner/pairs.json.before-partner-simple") === $copy]);
    same('migration: the units waiting for Mr. Backupsy\'s setup — those settings.ini lacks the partner line for', ['a1b2c3d4' => ['share:media', 'place']],
        partnerTestAs($M, 'return partnerMigratedPending();'));
    file_put_contents("$M[data]/unraid-backup/settings.ini", "[general]\ndumps_share = UnraidSecretaryOffice\n[partner \"a1b2c3d4\"]\nname = homeserver\n[share \"media\"]\nmode = snapshot\npartner = a1b2c3d4\n");
    same('migration: … applied for media (settings.ini has its line): the place still waits', ['a1b2c3d4' => ['place']], partnerTestAs($M, 'return partnerMigratedPending();'));
    file_put_contents("$M[data]/unraid-backup/settings.ini", "[general]\ndumps_share = UnraidSecretaryOffice\npartner_place = a1b2c3d4\n[partner \"a1b2c3d4\"]\nname = homeserver\n[share \"media\"]\nmode = snapshot\npartner = a1b2c3d4\n");
    same('migration: … both applied: nothing waits', [], partnerTestAs($M, 'return partnerMigratedPending();'));
    $steps = array_column(officeMigrateSteps(), 'version', 'id');
    same('migration: the step is registered for 1.60.0', '1.60.0', $steps['partner-simple'] ?? null);
    same('migration: no pairs.json — nothing to change', 'no pairs.json — nothing to change', partnerMigrateSimple("$tmp/nowhere"));

    // ---- two offices: A sends what its levels say, B keeps whatever comes
    $A = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/A");
    $B = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/B", 'vault');
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/unraid-backup/state/setup-plan.json", json_encode(['bases' => [['name' => 'tank', 'fs' => 'zfs', 'kind' => 'pool'], ['name' => 'hazel', 'fs' => 'zfs', 'kind' => 'pool']],
        'shares' => [['name' => 'appdata', 'layout' => 'single', 'locations' => 'tank'], ['name' => 'domains', 'layout' => 'single', 'locations' => 'tank'],
                     ['name' => 'docs', 'layout' => 'single', 'locations' => 'tank'], ['name' => 'UnraidSecretaryOffice', 'layout' => 'single', 'locations' => 'tank'],
                     ['name' => 'media', 'layout' => 'single', 'locations' => 'hazel'], ['name' => 'isos', 'layout' => 'overlay', 'locations' => 'tank, disk1']], 'vms' => []]));
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/unraid-backup/settings.ini", "[general]\ndumps_share = UnraidSecretaryOffice\n");
    file_put_contents("$A[root]/disks.ini", "[\"tank\"]\nname=\"tank\"\nspundown=\"0\"\n[\"hazel\"]\nname=\"hazel\"\nspundown=\"1\"\n");
    $target = fn (array $o) => ['php' => PHP_BINARY, 'door' => OFFICE_DIR . '/agent/partner-door.php', 'host_key' => $o['host'], 'auth_keys' => $o['keys'],
                                'env' => array_diff_key($o['env'], ['PATH' => 1]) + ['PATH' => '/usr/bin:/bin']];
    $dsOf = fn (array $names) => array_fill_keys($names, ['used' => 0]);
    partnerTestBin($A['bin'], ['pools' => ['tank', 'hazel'], 'ds' => $dsOf(['tank', 'tank/appdata', 'tank/domains', 'tank/docs', 'tank/UnraidSecretaryOffice', 'hazel', 'hazel/media'])],
        ['root@192.168.77.2' => $target($B)]);
    partnerTestBin($B['bin'], ['pools' => ['vault'], 'ds' => $dsOf(['vault'])], ['root@192.168.77.1' => $target($A)]);
    $as = fn (array $o, string $code) => partnerTestAs($o, $code);
    $made = $as($A, 'return partner_add(["step" => "do", "address" => "192.168.77.1", "port" => 22, "trust" => "mine"]);');
    $id = (string) ($made['id'] ?? '');
    same('units: BLOCK-A names every unit this server could send (an older partner\'s dialog) — the sleeping pool\'s and the split share left out', ['place', 'share:appdata', 'share:docs', 'share:domains'],
        partnerBlockDecode((string) ($made['block'] ?? ''), 'A')['units']);
    $acc = $as($B, 'return partner_accept(' . var_export(['step' => 'do', 'block' => (string) ($made['block'] ?? ''), 'confirm' => true, 'address' => '192.168.77.2', 'port' => 22,
        'trust' => 'mine', 'send_too' => false, 'receive' => ['pool' => 'vault', 'quota_gb' => 0, 'retention' => '7 4 6', 'wake' => false]], true) . ');');
    $fin = $as($A, 'return partner_finish(["step" => "do", "confirm" => true, "code" => ' . var_export((string) ($acc['code'] ?? ''), true) . ', "block" => '
        . var_export((string) ($acc['block'] ?? ''), true) . ', "receive" => null]);');
    same('units: paired — A reaches B', true, $fin['ask']['reachable'] ?? $fin);
    same('units: the pair on A — send only its rate; on B — the rules, no units', [['rate_mbit' => 0], ['pool' => 'vault', 'quota_gb' => 0, 'retention' => '7 4 6', 'wake' => true]],
        [$as($A, 'return partnerPairs()[0]["send"] ?? null;'), $as($B, 'return partnerPairs()[0]["receive"] ?? null;')]);
    $calls = fn () => array_values(array_map(fn ($c) => end($c), array_filter(partnerTestCalls($A['bin']), fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'ssh')));
    $calls();
    $cardA = fn () => $as($A, 'return partnerPublic()["pairs"][0];');
    $cardB = fn () => $as($B, 'return partnerPublic()["pairs"][0];');
    same('units: A\'s card — nothing sent yet (no level), B\'s — nothing received yet', [[], []], [$cardA()['send_units'] ?? null, $cardB()['i_keep_units'] ?? null]);
    // the levels in Mr. Backupsy's setup: the place and appdata to B
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/unraid-backup/settings.ini", "[general]\ndumps_share = UnraidSecretaryOffice\npartner_place = $id\n[partner \"$id\"]\nname = vault\naddress = 192.168.77.2\nport = 22\n"
        . "[share \"appdata\"]\nmode = snapshot\npartner = $id\n[share \"docs\"]\nmode = snapshot\n");
    same('units: A\'s card says what the levels send there', ['place', 'share:appdata'], $cardA()['send_units'] ?? null);
    same('units: partnerSendUnits — the pair\'s units from settings.ini, another pair none', [['place', 'share:appdata'], []], [$as($A, 'return partnerSendUnits("' . $id . '");'), $as($A, 'return partnerSendUnits("ffffffff");')]);
    // B's door takes any unit of A — one never named anywhere too
    $rc = partnerTestDoor($B, 'recv share:domains uso-backup-20261008-0200', 'SNAP:uso-backup-20261008-0200 whole', $id);
    same('units: B\'s door takes a unit nobody listed (the consent is the pairing)', 0, $rc['exit']);
    $rc = partnerTestDoor($B, 'recv place uso-backup-20261008-0200', 'SNAP:uso-backup-20261008-0200 whole', $id);
    same('units: … and the place', 0, $rc['exit']);
    $cb = $cardB();
    same('units: B\'s card — what it keeps of A, each new (first received within 7 days), the rules', [['place', 'share:domains'], [true, true], [false, false], 'vault'],
        [array_column($cb['i_keep_units'] ?? [], 'unit'), array_column($cb['i_keep_units'] ?? [], 'new'), array_column($cb['i_keep_units'] ?? [], 'stale'), $cb['receive']['pool'] ?? null]);
    check('units: B\'s first knock asked the Team Lead for his cards anew (the marker in RAM)', is_file("$B[run]/" . PARTNER_RESCAN_FILE));
    same('units: … taken once', [true, false], [$as($B, 'return partnerRescanDue();'), $as($B, 'return partnerRescanDue();')]);
    $st = partnerTestDoor($B, 'status', '', $id)['out'][0] ?? [];
    same('units: B\'s status — takes any unit, agreed = what it received', [true, ['place', 'share:domains'], []], [$st['takes_all'] ?? null, (function ($a) { sort($a); return $a; })($st['agreed'] ?? []), $st['wish'] ?? null]);
    // a unit stale (nothing received for 30 days), one new: as the record says
    $rec = json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$B[data]/partner/received/$id.json"), true);
    $rec['units']['share:domains']['time'] -= 40 * 86400;
    $rec['units']['share:domains']['first'] -= 60 * 86400;
    $as($B, 'partnerWritePrivate(partnerDir() . "/received/' . $id . '.json", ' . var_export($rec, true) . '); return true;');
    $cb = $cardB();
    same('units: a unit nothing came of for 40 days — stale, not new; the fresh one new', [['place', 'share:domains'], [true, false], [false, true]],
        [array_column($cb['i_keep_units'] ?? [], 'unit'), array_column($cb['i_keep_units'] ?? [], 'new'), array_column($cb['i_keep_units'] ?? [], 'stale')]);
    same('units: partnerReceivedUnits — a record up to 1.59 (no first): the last time counts as the first; an odd name left out', [['share:x', true, false]],
        array_map(fn ($u) => [$u['unit'], $u['new'], $u['stale']], partnerReceivedUnits(['units' => ['share:x' => ['snap' => 's', 'time' => time() - 60, 'snaps' => 1], '../y' => ['time' => 1]]], time())));
    // the mutual watch: B takes all — nothing offered; the card knows B's status
    $as($A, 'return partnerWatch(fn () => false, fn () => true);');
    same('units: the watch — ping and status, no offer (B takes any unit)', ['ping', 'status'], $calls());
    $ca = $cardA();
    same('units: A\'s card — B\'s status: takes all, keeps place and domains; not an older office', [true, ['place', 'share:domains'], false],
        [$ca['they_keep']['takes_all'] ?? null, (function ($a) { sort($a); return $a; })($ca['they_keep']['agreed'] ?? []), $ca['older'] ?? null]);
    check('units: nothing of a key in the cards', !str_contains(json_encode($ca) . json_encode($cb), 'ssh-ed25519'));

    // ---- an older partner (its status without takes_all keeps only what its Team Lead agreed to): the watch offers the units
    $ask = ['time' => time(), 'reachable' => true, 'answer' => ['array' => 'started', 'night' => false, 'v' => '1.59.0', 'time' => time()], 'why' => null,
            'status' => ['agreed' => ['place'], 'takes_all' => false]];
    same('units: an older partner lacking appdata — an offer is due; one that takes all, or agreed to everything, or knows no agreed, not',
        [true, false, false, false], $as($A, '$p = partnerPair("' . $id . '"); return [partnerOfferDue($p, ' . var_export($ask['status'], true) . '), partnerOfferDue($p, ["agreed" => [], "takes_all" => true]),'
            . ' partnerOfferDue($p, ["agreed" => ["place", "share:appdata"], "takes_all" => false]), partnerOfferDue($p, ["agreed" => null, "takes_all" => false])];'));
    $r = $as($A, '$p = partnerPair("' . $id . '"); [$p, $e] = partnerUnitsFollow($p, ' . var_export($ask, true) . ', []); return $e;');
    same('units: … the watch offered the units through B\'s door (B of today takes them whole)', [true, []], [$r['offer']['ok'] ?? null, $r['offer']['pending'] ?? null]);
    same('units: … one door call: offer with every unit the levels send', ['offer place share:appdata'], $calls());
    partnerWritePrivate("$A[data]/partner/state.json", ['pairs' => [$id => ['status' => ['agreed' => ['place'], 'takes_all' => false, 'units' => []], 'status_time' => time(),
        'offer' => ['time' => time(), 'ok' => true, 'why' => null, 'pending' => ['share:appdata']]]]]);
    $ca = $cardA();
    same('units: A\'s card of an older partner — older, what it keeps, the last offer', [true, ['place'], ['share:appdata']], [$ca['older'] ?? null, $ca['they_keep']['agreed'] ?? null, $ca['offer']['pending'] ?? null]);
    same('units: the offer needs a key and units', ['no_key', 'no_key'], [partnerOffer(['my_key' => null] + partnerTestPair($id), ['place'])['why'], partnerOffer(partnerTestPair($id), [])['why']]);

    // ---- a pair that keeps nothing here can't offer; the array stopped — no offer
    same('units: a pair that keeps nothing here can\'t offer', 'not_receiving', partnerTestDoor($A, 'offer place', '', $id)['out'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    file_put_contents("$B[root]/var.ini", "fsState=\"Stopped\"\n");
    same('units: the array stopped — no offer', 'array_stopped', partnerTestDoor($B, 'offer place', '', $id)['out'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    file_put_contents("$B[root]/var.ini", "fsState=\"Started\"\n");

    // ---- the partnership ends: what A named at B's door goes with it
    partnerTestDoor($B, 'offer place share:appdata', '', $id);
    check('units: what A named there before the end', file_exists("$B[data]/partner/wishes/$id.json"));
    $as($B, 'return partner_end(["id" => ' . var_export($id, true) . ']);');
    check('units: the end takes it along', !file_exists("$B[data]/partner/wishes/$id.json"));

    // the strings the pages ask for
    $en = langFile(OFFICE_DIR . '/public/desks/caretaker/lang/en.json');
    foreach (['errors.partner_not_sending', 'partner.i_send', 'partner.i_keep', 'partner.consent', 'partner.unit_new', 'partner.unit_stale', 'partner.older'] as $key) {
        check("units: caretaker.$key", isset($en[$key]));
    }
    foreach (['partner.change', 'partner.wish', 'partner.keep_less', 'partner.window', 'check.partner_wish'] as $key) {
        check("units: caretaker.$key gone", !isset($en[$key]));
    }
    foreach (['en', 'de', 'it', 'fr', 'es'] as $l) {
        $bk = langFile(OFFICE_DIR . "/public/desks/backup/lang/$l.json");
        check("units: backup $l partner.why.not_agreed, the levels, the preset", isset($bk['partner.why.not_agreed'], $bk['partner.why_short.not_agreed'], $bk['setup.level.partner'], $bk['setup.level.partner_kopia'],
            $bk['setup.preset.partner'], $bk['setup.preset.kopia_partner_tick'], $bk['setup.mode.snapshot_partner'], $bk['setup.mode.kopia_partner']));
    }
    hardeningRm($tmp);
}

/** agent.sh partner_release at the array stop: the door's registered processes end, the records go */
function testPartnerRelease(): void
{
    $tmp = hardeningTmp('partner-release');
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp) . '/*');
    @mkdir("$tmp/run/partner", 0700, true);
    @mkdir("$tmp/agent", 0700, true);
    @mkdir("$tmp/sbin", 0700, true);
    file_put_contents("$tmp/agent/partner-door.php", "trap 'exit 0' TERM\nsleep 30 & wait\n");
    $start = function (array $cmd) {
        $p = proc_open($cmd, [0 => ['file', '/dev/null', 'r'], 1 => ['file', '/dev/null', 'w'], 2 => ['file', '/dev/null', 'w']], $pipes);
        usleep(100000);
        return $p;
    };
    $door = $start(['/bin/bash', "$tmp/agent/partner-door.php"]);
    $zfs = $start(['/bin/bash', '-c', 'exec -a /usr/sbin/zfs /bin/sleep 30']);       // a process called zfs
    $other = $start(['/bin/sleep', '30']);
    $pid = fn ($p) => proc_get_status($p)['pid'];
    file_put_contents("$tmp/run/partner/door-{$pid($door)}.json", json_encode(['pid' => $pid($door), 'children' => [$pid($zfs), $pid($other)]]));
    file_put_contents("$tmp/run/partner/door-{$pid($other)}.json", json_encode(['pid' => $pid($other), 'children' => []]));    // not a door: left alone
    $agent = escapeshellarg(OFFICE_DIR . '/plugin/scripts/agent.sh');
    $t0 = microtime(true);
    $out = trim((string) shell_exec('bash -c ' . escapeshellarg("source $agent; RUN=" . escapeshellarg("$tmp/run") . '; LOG=' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/agent.log") . '; partner_release; echo "rc=$?"') . ' 2>&1'));
    $took = microtime(true) - $t0;
    usleep(200000);
    same('partner release: ends without a word', 'rc=0', $out);
    same('partner release: the door and its zfs recv ended, anything else left alone', [false, false, true],
        [proc_get_status($door)['running'], proc_get_status($zfs)['running'], proc_get_status($other)['running']]);
    check('partner release: within 5 s', $took < 5.5, (string) round($took, 1));
    same('partner release: the records gone', [], glob("$tmp/run/partner/door-*.json"));
    check('partner release: said in the log', str_contains((string) @file_get_contents("$tmp/agent.log"), 'array stopping: a partner\'s transfer ended (2 process(es) of the door)'));
    proc_terminate($other);
    foreach ([$door, $zfs, $other] as $p) {
        proc_close($p);
    }
    $out = trim((string) shell_exec('bash -c ' . escapeshellarg("source $agent; RUN=" . escapeshellarg("$tmp/run") . '; LOG=' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/agent2.log") . '; partner_release; echo "rc=$?"') . ' 2>&1'));
    same('partner release: nothing registered — nothing done, nothing said', ['rc=0', false], [$out, is_file("$tmp/agent2.log")]);
    check('partner release: called at the array stop, beside backup_release', (bool) preg_match('/partner_release[^\n]*\n\s*backup_release/', (string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_DIR . '/plugin/scripts/agent.sh')));
    hardeningRm($tmp);
}
/** The door's way back (send-back, its -t form) and the restore tickets' door: verbs, units, expiry, the tidy */
function testPartnerSendBack(): void
{
    if (posix_geteuid() !== 0) {
        check('partner send-back: root only — not run here', true);
        return;
    }
    $tmp = hardeningTmp('partner-sendback');
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp) . '/*');
    $B = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/B");
    $id = 'a1b2c3d4';
    $ds = 'tank/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id/share-appdata";
    $vm = 'tank/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id/vm-Debian_VM";
    $snap = fn (int $c) => ['userrefs' => 0, 'used' => 10, 'written' => 10, 'creation' => $c];
    $st = ['pools' => ['tank'], 'ds' => ['tank' => ['used' => 0], 'tank/' . PARTNER_PARENT => ['used' => 0], 'tank/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id" => ['used' => 0],
           $ds => ['used' => 0], $vm => ['used' => 0], 'tank/appdata' => ['used' => 0]],
           'snaps' => ["$ds@uso-backup-20261001-0200" => $snap(1), "$ds@uso-backup-20261002-0200" => $snap(2), "$vm@uso-backup-20261002-0200" => $snap(3),
                       'tank/appdata@uso-backup-20261002-0200' => $snap(4)],
           'tokens' => ['1-aaaaaaaa11-c8-789c0123456789' => "$ds@uso-backup-20261002-0200", '1-bbbbbbbb22-c8-789c0123456789' => 'tank/appdata@uso-backup-20261002-0200',
                        '1-cccccccc33-c8-789c0123456789' => "$ds@manual-snap"]];
    $st['snaps']["$ds@manual-snap"] = $snap(5);
    partnerTestBin($B['bin'], $st);
    $pairsFile = "$B[data]/partner/pairs.json";
    partnerPairsWrite([partnerTestPair($id), partnerTestPair('b2c3d4e5', ['their_key' => null, 'receive' => null])], $pairsFile);
    $log = fn () => (string) @file_get_contents("$B[data]/partner/door.log");
    $sends = function () use ($B): array {
        $c = array_values(array_filter(partnerTestCalls($B['bin']), fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'mbuffer' || ($c[0] === 'zfs' && ($c[1] ?? '') === 'send' && !preg_grep('/^-n/', $c))));
        usort($c, fn ($a, $b) => strcmp(json_encode($b), json_encode($a)));      // zfs before mbuffer, whichever wrote first
        return $c;
    };

    // ---- the whole copy back
    $r = partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200');
    same('send-back: the stream on stdout, ok before (with the size) and after on stderr', [0, "SNAP:uso-backup-20261002-0200 whole\n", ['ok' => true, 'size' => 110], true],
        [$r['exit'], explode('{', $r['raw'])[0], $r['err'][0] ?? null, ($r['err'][1]['ok'] ?? null) === true && isset($r['err'][1]['seconds'])]);
    same('send-back: zfs send -L -c of the pair\'s own dataset, through mbuffer', [['zfs', 'send', '-L', '-c', "$ds@uso-backup-20261002-0200"], ['mbuffer', '-q', '-s', '128k', '-m', '256M']], $sends());
    check('send-back: in the door\'s log', str_contains($log(), "send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200 (whole) <- $ds") && str_contains($log(), 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200 done'));
    same('send-back: no record of a transfer left', [], glob("$B[run]/partner/door-*.json"));
    $r = partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200 uso-backup-20261001-0200');
    same('send-back: incremental', [0, "SNAP:uso-backup-20261002-0200 from uso-backup-20261001-0200\n"], [$r['exit'], explode('{', $r['raw'])[0]]);
    same('send-back: … zfs send -i', [['zfs', 'send', '-L', '-c', '-i', "$ds@uso-backup-20261001-0200", "$ds@uso-backup-20261002-0200"], ['mbuffer', '-q', '-s', '128k', '-m', '256M']], $sends());
    same('send-back: a VM\'s copy', 0, partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back vm:Debian_VM uso-backup-20261002-0200')['exit']);
    $sends();

    // ---- resumed: the token is the puller's — only one that names this unit's dataset and an engine snapshot
    $r = partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back share:appdata -t 1-aaaaaaaa11-c8-789c0123456789');
    same('send-back -t: zfs send -t', [0, "SNAP:uso-backup-20261002-0200 whole resumed\n", 110], [$r['exit'], explode('{', $r['raw'])[0], $r['err'][0]['size'] ?? null]);
    same('send-back -t: … the token sent as it came', [['zfs', 'send', '-t', '1-aaaaaaaa11-c8-789c0123456789'], ['mbuffer', '-q', '-s', '128k', '-m', '256M']], $sends());
    $long = '1-' . str_repeat('ab12', 700);
    foreach (['send-back share:appdata -t 1-bbbbbbbb22-c8-789c0123456789' => 'token_other', 'send-back share:appdata -t 1-cccccccc33-c8-789c0123456789' => 'token_other',
              'send-back vm:Debian_VM -t 1-aaaaaaaa11-c8-789c0123456789' => 'token_other', 'send-back share:appdata -t 1-dddddddd44-c8-789c0123456789' => 'bad_token',
              "send-back share:appdata -t $long" => 'bad_token', 'send-back share:appdata -t short' => 'bad_token'] as $cmd => $why) {
        $r = partnerTestDoor($B, $cmd);
        same('send-back -t refused — ' . substr($cmd, 10, 50), [1, $why, ''], [$r['exit'], $r['err'][0]['why'] ?? $r['raw'], explode('{', $r['raw'])[0]]);
    }
    same('send-back -t: none of those sent a byte', [], $sends());

    // ---- refusals
    $bad = [
        'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261009-0200' => 'no_snapshot', 'send-back share:appdata manual-snap' => 'bad_snap',
        'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200 uso-backup-20260101-0200' => 'need_full', 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261001-0200 uso-backup-20261002-0200' => 'need_full',
        'send-back share:system uso-backup-20261002-0200' => 'no_snapshot', 'send-back place uso-backup-20261002-0200' => 'no_snapshot',
        'send-back share:appdata' => 'malformed', 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200 -t' => 'bad_snap', 'send-back share:appdata -t 1-aaaa;id' => 'malformed',
        'send-back share:appdata -t ' . str_repeat('a', 4100) => 'malformed', 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200 ' . str_repeat('a', 300) => 'malformed',
        'list share:appdata ' . str_repeat('a', 300) => 'malformed', 'send-back tank/appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200' => 'malformed', 'send-back -F uso-backup-20261002-0200' => 'bad_unit',
    ];
    foreach ($bad as $cmd => $why) {
        $r = partnerTestDoor($B, $cmd);
        same('send-back refused — ' . substr($cmd, 0, 70), [true, $why], [$r['exit'] !== 0, (array_merge($r['out'], $r['err'])[0]['why'] ?? $r['raw'])]);
    }
    same('send-back: a pair that keeps nothing here', 'not_receiving', partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200', '', 'b2c3d4e5')['err'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    @mkdir("$B[run]/partner", 0700, true);
    $hold = fopen("$B[run]/partner/$id.lock", 'c');
    flock($hold, LOCK_EX);
    same('send-back: one transfer per pair — busy', 'busy', partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200')['err'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    flock($hold, LOCK_UN);
    fclose($hold);
    $z = json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json"), true);
    $z['send_fail'] = true;
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json", json_encode($z));
    $r = partnerTestDoor($B, 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200');
    same('send-back: zfs send failing — said after', [1, ['ok' => true, 'size' => 110], 'send_failed'], [$r['exit'], $r['err'][0] ?? null, $r['err'][1]['why'] ?? null]);
    $z['send_fail'] = false;
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json", json_encode($z));
    $sends();
    same('send-back: nothing written, renamed or destroyed by any of it', [], array_values(array_filter(partnerTestCalls($B['bin']), fn ($c) => in_array($c[1] ?? '', ['recv', 'create', 'destroy', 'set', 'rename'], true))));

    // ---- restore tickets: a line of their own, ping / list / send-back / quota on the pair's copies, until expires
    $t1 = 'c3d4e5f6';
    $t2 = 'd4e5f6a7';
    $now = time();
    $ticket = fn (string $tid, int $expires, array $over = []) => $over + ['id' => $tid, 'of' => $id, 'name' => 'newbox', 'address' => '192.168.77.9', 'from' => '192.168.77.9',
        'key' => partnerFingerprint(partnerTestKey()), 'created' => $expires - PARTNER_TICKET_DAYS * 86400, 'expires' => $expires, 'units' => ['share:appdata']];
    partnerTestAs($B, 'partnerTicketsWrite(' . var_export([$ticket($t1, $now + 3600), $ticket($t2, $now - 60)], true) . '); return true;');
    same('tickets.json root only', 0600, fileperms("$B[data]/partner/tickets.json") & 0777);
    $T = fn (string $cmd, string $tid = 'c3d4e5f6', array $env = []) => partnerTestDoor($B, $cmd, '', "ticket-$tid", $env);
    $r = $T('ping');
    same('ticket: ping', [0, true, $t1], [$r['exit'], $r['out'][0]['ok'] ?? null, $r['out'][0]['pair'] ?? null]);
    $r = $T('list share:appdata');
    same('ticket: list of the unit it names', ['uso-backup-20261001-0200', 'uso-backup-20261002-0200'], array_column($r['out'][0]['snaps'] ?? [], 'name') ?: $r['raw']);
    same('ticket: quota (the pair\'s)', [0, true], [$T('quota')['exit'], $T('quota')['out'][0]['ok'] ?? null]);
    $r = $T('send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200');
    same('ticket: send-back', [0, "SNAP:uso-backup-20261002-0200 whole\n"], [$r['exit'], explode('{', $r['raw'])[0]]);
    foreach (['status' => 'ticket_verb', 'recv share:appdata uso-backup-20261003-0200' => 'ticket_verb', 'resume share:appdata' => 'ticket_verb',
              'list vm:Debian_VM' => 'unit_not_agreed', 'send-back vm:Debian_VM uso-backup-20261002-0200' => 'unit_not_agreed', 'rm -rf /' => 'malformed'] as $cmd => $why) {
        $r = $T($cmd);
        same("ticket: refused — $cmd", [true, $why], [$r['exit'] !== 0, array_merge($r['out'], $r['err'])[0]['why'] ?? $r['raw']]);
    }
    $r = $T('list share:appdata', $t2);
    same('ticket expired — refused, with the server\'s time', [1, 'ticket_expired', true], [$r['exit'], $r['out'][0]['why'] ?? null, abs(($r['out'][0]['time'] ?? 0) - time()) < 30]);
    same('ticket expired — its ping too', 'ticket_expired', $T('ping', $t2)['out'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    same('ticket expired — its send-back too (stderr)', 'ticket_expired', $T('send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261002-0200', $t2)['err'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    file_put_contents("$tmp/stopped.ini", "fsState=\"Stopped\"\n");
    same('ticket: ping while the array is stopped — RAM and flash only', [0, 'stopped'], [$T('ping', $t2, ['OFFICE_VAR_INI' => "$tmp/stopped.ini"])['exit'],
        $T('ping', $t2, ['OFFICE_VAR_INI' => "$tmp/stopped.ini"])['out'][0]['array'] ?? null]);
    same('ticket: one the holder doesn\'t know', 'no_ticket', $T('list share:appdata', 'eeeeeeee')['out'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    foreach (['ticket-', 'ticket-A1B2C3D4', 'ticket-a1b2c3d4x', 'tickets-a1b2c3d4', 'ticket-../x'] as $arg) {
        same('ticket: no pair from the line ' . $arg, 'no_pair', partnerTestDoor($B, 'ping', '', $arg)['out'][0]['why'] ?? null);
    }
    check('ticket: refusals counted under the ticket\'s id', is_file("$B[run]/partner/refused-$t1.json") && is_file("$B[run]/partner/refused-$t2.json"));
    partnerTestAs($B, 'partnerTicketsWrite(' . var_export([$ticket($t1, $now + 3600, ['of' => 'f0f0f0f0'])], true) . '); return true;');
    same('ticket: the pair it was given for is gone', 'no_pair', $T('list share:appdata')['out'][0]['why'] ?? null);

    // ---- the line, and the tidy at the agent's start and once a day
    $k1 = partnerTestKey();
    $l1 = partnerTicketLine($t1, '192.168.77.9', $k1, strtotime('2026-10-15 12:00 UTC'));
    same('ticket: its line — restrict, sshd\'s expiry-time in UTC, from=, the door with ticket-<id>, uso-ticket:<id>',
        'restrict,expiry-time="202610151200Z",from="192.168.77.9",command="' . PARTNER_DOOR . " ticket-$t1\" $k1 uso-ticket:$t1", $l1);
    check('ticket: its line is a ticket\'s, not a pair\'s', partnerTicketLineIsOurs($l1, $t1) && !partnerLineIsOurs($l1) && !partnerTicketLineIsOurs($l1, $t2));
    $benj = "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBenjBenjBenjBenjBenjBenjBenjBenjBenjBenj benj@MacBook\n";
    $pairLine = partnerDoorLine($id, '192.168.77.1', partnerTestKey());
    $l2 = partnerTicketLine($t2, '192.168.77.9', partnerTestKey(), $now - 60);
    $l3 = partnerTicketLine('f1f2f3f4', '192.168.77.9', partnerTestKey(), $now + 999);
    file_put_contents($B['keys'], $benj . $pairLine . "\n" . $l1 . "\n" . $l2 . "\n" . $l3 . "\n");
    partnerTestAs($B, 'partnerTicketsWrite(' . var_export([$ticket($t1, $now + 3600), $ticket($t2, $now - 60)], true) . '); return true;');
    $gone = partnerTestAs($B, 'return partnerTicketsTidy();');
    same('ticket tidy: the expired one and one without its ticket went — the rest byte for byte', [2, $benj . $pairLine . "\n" . $l1 . "\n"], [$gone, file_get_contents($B['keys'])]);
    same('ticket tidy: tickets.json keeps the living one', [$t1], array_column(partnerTestAs($B, 'return partnerTickets();'), 'id'));
    same('ticket tidy: nothing more the second time', 0, partnerTestAs($B, 'return partnerTicketsTidy();'));
    same('ticket: its line read back', $l1, partnerAuthKeysLine($t1, $B['keys'], true));
    $strip = partnerAuthKeysStrip(file_get_contents($B['keys']));
    same('authorized_keys: every line of the office\'s out at once (the .plg\'s remove) — pairs and tickets', $benj, $strip);
    $plg = (string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_DIR . '/plugin/unraid-secretary-office.plg');
    $one = preg_match("/php -r '(umask\\(077\\);.*?)' \"\\\$keys\"/s", $plg, $m) ? $m[1] : '';
    exec(escapeshellarg(PHP_BINARY) . ' -r ' . escapeshellarg($one) . ' ' . escapeshellarg($B['keys']));
    same('authorized_keys: the .plg\'s remove takes the tickets\' lines too', $benj, file_get_contents($B['keys']));
    check('the .plg\'s remove looks for the tickets\' mark', str_contains($plg, "grep -q 'uso-\\(partner\\|ticket\\):[0-9a-f]\\{8\\}'"));
    try {
        partnerAuthKeysEdit($t1, $pairLine, $B['keys'], true);
        check('authorized_keys: a pair\'s line refused as a ticket\'s', false);
    } catch (Problem $e) {
        same('authorized_keys: a pair\'s line refused as a ticket\'s', 'partner_shape', $e->key);
    }
    hardeningRm($tmp);
}

/**
 * Two offices for Mr. Restori across servers: A sends share:appdata, vm:Debian_VM and place to B (pair a1b2c3d4); B's
 * door keeps them in vault/UnraidSecretaryOffice-partners/a1b2c3d4/…; ssh, zfs, pv, mbuffer, mount played by stand-ins.
 */
function restorePartnerTestPair(string $tmp, array $sendUnits = ['share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM', 'place']): array
{
    $id = 'a1b2c3d4';
    $A = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/A");
    $B = partnerTestOffice("$tmp/B", 'vault');
    $target = fn (array $o) => ['php' => PHP_BINARY, 'door' => OFFICE_DIR . '/agent/partner-door.php', 'host_key' => $o['host'], 'auth_keys' => $o['keys'],
                                'env' => array_diff_key($o['env'], ['PATH' => 1]) + ['PATH' => '/usr/bin:/bin']];
    $pd = 'vault/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id";
    $snap = fn (int $c, int $ref = 1000) => ['userrefs' => 0, 'used' => 10, 'written' => 10, 'creation' => $c];
    partnerTestBin($A['bin'], ['pools' => ['tank'], 'ds' => array_fill_keys(['tank', 'tank/appdata', 'tank/domains', 'tank/domains/Debian_VM', 'tank/UnraidSecretaryOffice'], ['used' => 0]),
        'avail' => ['tank' => 50 * 1024 ** 3]], ['root@192.168.77.2' => $target($B)]);
    partnerTestBin($B['bin'], ['pools' => ['vault'], 'ds' => array_fill_keys(['vault', "vault/" . PARTNER_PARENT, $pd, "$pd/share-appdata", "$pd/vm-Debian_VM", "$pd/place"], ['used' => 0]),
        'snaps' => ["$pd/share-appdata@uso-backup-20261006-0200" => $snap(1791250000), "$pd/share-appdata@uso-backup-20261007-0200" => $snap(1791336000),
                    "$pd/vm-Debian_VM@uso-backup-20261007-0200" => $snap(1791336001), "$pd/place@uso-backup-20261007-0200" => $snap(1791336002)]], ['root@192.168.77.1' => $target($A)]);
    $pubA = partnerTestKey();
    file_put_contents("$A[flash]/$id.key", "not a real key\n");
    file_put_contents("$A[flash]/$id.key.pub", "$pubA uso-partner:$id\n");
    file_put_contents("$A[flash]/$id.known", partnerKnownText('192.168.77.2', 22, [trim(file_get_contents($B['host']))]));
    file_put_contents($B['keys'], partnerDoorLine($id, '192.168.77.1', $pubA) . "\n");
    partnerTestAs($A, 'partnerPairsWrite([' . var_export(partnerTestPair($id, ['address' => '192.168.77.2', 'my_key' => partnerFingerprint($pubA), 'their_key' => null,
        'receive' => null]), true) . ']); return true;');
    partnerTestAs($B, 'partnerPairsWrite([' . var_export(partnerTestPair($id, ['address' => '192.168.77.1', 'my_key' => null,
        'their_key' => partnerFingerprint($pubA), 'receive' => ['pool' => 'vault', 'quota_gb' => 0, 'retention' => '7 4 6', 'wake' => false]]), true) . ']); return true;');
    // what B's door received of A (1.60: the pair names no units — the record says what is held here)
    partnerTestAs($B, 'partnerWritePrivate(partnerDir() . "/received/' . $id . '.json", ["pair" => "' . $id . '", "units" => ["share:appdata" => ["snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "bytes" => 10, "seconds" => 1, "time" => 1791336000, "snaps" => 2, "first" => 1791250000],'
        . ' "vm:Debian_VM" => ["snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "bytes" => 10, "seconds" => 1, "time" => 1791336001, "snaps" => 1, "first" => 1791336001],'
        . ' "place" => ["snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "bytes" => 10, "seconds" => 1, "time" => 1791336002, "snaps" => 1, "first" => 1791336002]], "used_bytes" => 30, "time" => 1791336002]); return true;');
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/unraid-backup/state/partner-sent.json", json_encode([$id => ['share:appdata' => ['snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'dataset' => 'tank/appdata'],
        'vm:Debian_VM' => ['snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'dataset' => 'tank/domains/Debian_VM'], 'place' => ['snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'dataset' => 'tank/UnraidSecretaryOffice']]]));
    // what A sends: the levels in Mr. Backupsy's setup (settings.ini), since 1.60 — not the pair
    $ini = "[general]\ndumps_share = UnraidSecretaryOffice\n" . (in_array('place', $sendUnits, true) ? "partner_place = $id\n" : '') . "[partner \"$id\"]\nname = vault\naddress = 192.168.77.2\nport = 22\n";
    foreach ($sendUnits as $u) {
        if (preg_match('/^(share|vm):(.+)$/', $u, $m)) {
            $ini .= "[$m[1] \"$m[2]\"]\nmode = snapshot\npartner = $id\n";
        }
    }
    file_put_contents("$A[data]/unraid-backup/settings.ini", $ini);
    @mkdir("$tmp/A/restored", 0755, true);
    $A['pre'] = 'date_default_timezone_set("UTC"); $GLOBALS["rs"]["restored_root"] = ' . var_export("$tmp/A/restored", true) . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["mounts_file"] = ' . var_export("$A[bin]/mounts", true)
        . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["var_ini"] = ' . var_export("$A[root]/var.ini", true) . ';';
    return [$A, $B, $id];
}

/** Mr. Restori across servers: «At <partner>» (the look job, held.json), the plan kind partner, the pull, its undo, a resume, the array stop */
function testRestorePartner(): void
{
    if (posix_geteuid() !== 0) {
        check('restore partner: root only — not run here', true);
        return;
    }
    $tmp = hardeningTmp('restore-partner');
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp) . '/*');
    [$A, $B, $id] = restorePartnerTestPair($tmp);
    $as = fn (string $code) => partnerTestAs($A, $A['pre'] . $code);
    $zfsA = fn () => json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$A[bin]/zfs.json"), true);
    $at = fn (int $ago) => gmdate('Ymd-His', time() - $ago);        // a preview's stamp: within the last day (rsStampOf(); the offices run in UTC)
    $stamp = $at(7200);

    // ---- «At <partner>»: the look job asks the door (list per unit), keeps it in held.json
    same('restore partner: the sources — the pair I send to (what settings.ini sends: the place first, as the engine orders it)', [[$id, 'pair', ['place', 'share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']]],
        array_map(fn ($s) => [$s['id'], $s['kind'], $s['units']], $as('return array_map(fn ($s) => array_diff_key($s, ["pair" => 1]), rspSources());')));
    same('restore partner: the look job', 0, $as('return rspLookJob([]);'));
    $held = json_decode((string) @file_get_contents("$A[data]/partner/$id/held.json"), true);
    same('restore partner: held.json — what B keeps of mine, with looked', [true, ['uso-backup-20261006-0200', 'uso-backup-20261007-0200'], ['uso-backup-20261007-0200'], true],
        [is_int($held['looked'] ?? null), array_column($held['units']['share:appdata'] ?? [], 'name'), array_column($held['units']['place'] ?? [], 'name'), $held['reachable'] ?? null]);
    same('restore partner: held.json root only', [0600, 0700], [fileperms("$A[data]/partner/$id/held.json") & 0777, fileperms("$A[data]/partner/$id") & 0777]);
    $st = $as('return rspState();');
    same('restore partner: his state — the place first, newest moment first', [['place', 'share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM'], 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 1791336000],
        [array_column($st[0]['units'] ?? [], 'unit'), $st[0]['units'][1]['snaps'][0]['name'] ?? null, $st[0]['units'][1]['newest'] ?? null]);
    check('restore partner: nothing of a key in his state', !str_contains(json_encode($st), 'ssh-ed25519') && !str_contains(json_encode($st), 'SHA256:'));
    same('restore partner: the chip «at <partner>» of an app in appdata', [['id' => $id, 'name' => 'homeserver', 'unit' => 'share:appdata', 'newest' => 1791336000, 'n' => 2]],
        $as('return rspChips(rspState(), ["appdata", "media"]);'));
    same('restore partner: … of a VM by its own unit', ['vm:Debian_VM'], array_column($as('return rspChips(rspState(), ["domains"], "Debian_VM");'), 'unit'));
    // unreachable: what was known stays, «as of»
    $t = json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$A[bin]/targets.json"), true);
    file_put_contents("$A[bin]/targets.json", json_encode([]));
    $as('rspLookJob([]); return true;');
    $held2 = json_decode((string) @file_get_contents("$A[data]/partner/$id/held.json"), true);
    same('restore partner: unreachable — what was known stays, looked stays, tried moves on', [false, 'unreachable', $held['looked'], 2],
        [$held2['reachable'] ?? null, $held2['why'] ?? null, $held2['looked'] ?? null, count($held2['units']['share:appdata'] ?? [])]);
    file_put_contents("$A[bin]/targets.json", json_encode($t));
    $as('rspLookJob([]); return true;');
    // the partner answers but no longer knows the pair (set up anew, 1.65.6): what it said it keeps is from then — the
    // units unknown now, no moment and no chip offered, a plan refused (its door would refuse the pull)
    $heldFile = "$A[data]/partner/$id/held.json";
    $heldOk = (string) file_get_contents($heldFile);
    file_put_contents($heldFile, json_encode(['reachable' => false, 'why' => 'no_pair'] + json_decode($heldOk, true)));
    $np = $as('return rspState();')[0] ?? [];
    same('restore partner: no_pair — the units unknown now, no moment offered, the why for the page', ['no_pair', [[], [], []], [false, false, false]],
        [$np['why'] ?? null, array_column($np['units'] ?? [], 'snaps'), array_column($np['units'] ?? [], 'known')]);
    same('restore partner: no_pair — no chip «at <partner>», a plan refused with its own reason', [[], 'restore_partner_no_pair'],
        [$as('return rspChips(rspState(), ["appdata", "media"]);'),
         $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null]);
    file_put_contents($heldFile, $heldOk);
    // a look that throws: the pid file and the lock go all the same (review 2026-10-09)
    same('restore partner: the look job throws — no pid file left, the lock free again, the next look runs', [true, false, true, 0],
        $as('$GLOBALS["rspLookOne"] = function () { throw new RuntimeException("boom"); }; $threw = false;'
            . ' try { rspLookJob([]); } catch (RuntimeException $e) { $threw = true; } unset($GLOBALS["rspLookOne"]);'
            . ' $h = fopen(partnerRunDir() . "/look.lock", "c"); $free = flock($h, LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB); flock($h, LOCK_UN); fclose($h);'
            . ' return [$threw, is_file(rspPidFile()), $free, rspLookJob([])];'));
    same('restore partner: «Look again» — a file in RAM for his tick', [true, true], [$as('return rspWantLook()["ok"];'), is_file("$A[run]/restore-partner.want")]);

    // ---- the plan: beside, never over; the steps; sizes; what comes after
    $plan = $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $stamp . '"]);');
    same('restore partner: the plan — pull, then mount read-only', [['pull', 'mount'], "tank/appdata.restored-$stamp", false, "$tmp/A/restored/homeserver-share-appdata-$stamp"],
        [array_column($plan['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), $plan['steps'][0]['dataset'] ?? null, $plan['steps'][0]['resume'] ?? null, $plan['steps'][1]['path'] ?? null]);
    same('restore partner: … nothing blocks, sizes from the partner and the pool', [[], 1000 > 0, 50 * 1024 ** 3], [$plan['blockers'] ?? null, ($plan['sizes']['need'] ?? -1) >= 0, $plan['sizes']['free'] ?? null]);
    same('restore partner: … said: beside, then «Restore…» of a folder in /mnt/user/appdata, how to remove it', [true, '/mnt/user/appdata', true],
        [in_array('note.partner_beside', array_column($plan['notes'] ?? [], 'key'), true), ($plan['after'][0]['params']['path'] ?? null),
         in_array('after.partner_drop', array_column($plan['after'] ?? [], 'key'), true)]);
    same('restore partner: … a moment it doesn\'t hold — blocked', 'restore_partner_no_snap',
        $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261009-0200"]);')['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null);
    same('restore partner: … a unit I don\'t send there — unknown', 'unknown_target',
        $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:media", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['problem'] ?? null);
    same('restore partner: … a path as a unit — unknown', 'unknown_target',
        $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "../../etc", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['problem'] ?? null);
    // the VM: the place comes along when held there, else the plain sentence
    $vm = $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $stamp . '"]);');
    same('restore partner: a VM — its disks and its package (the place) come back together', [['pull', 'mount', 'pull', 'mount'], ['vm:Debian_VM', 'place'],
        "tank/domains/Debian_VM.restored-$stamp", true], [array_column($vm['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), array_values(array_filter(array_column($vm['steps'] ?? [], 'unit'))),
        $vm['steps'][0]['dataset'] ?? null, in_array('note.partner_place_too', array_column($vm['notes'] ?? [], 'key'), true)]);
    [$A2, , ] = restorePartnerTestPair("$tmp/nopkg", ['share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']);
    partnerTestAs($A2, $A2['pre'] . 'rspLookJob([]); return true;');
    $vm2 = partnerTestAs($A2, $A2['pre'] . 'return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);');
    same('restore partner: a VM whose place isn\'t at the partner — only the disks, said plainly', [['pull', 'mount'], true, true],
        [array_column($vm2['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), in_array('note.partner_no_package', array_column($vm2['notes'] ?? [], 'key'), true), ($vm2['notes'][0]['warn'] ?? false) || true]);
    // a unit no longer sent but still agreed there (its status' agreed, the mutual watch's): still offered, the look asks for it
    [$A3, , ] = restorePartnerTestPair("$tmp/agreed", ['share:appdata']);
    $as3 = fn (string $code) => partnerTestAs($A3, $A3['pre'] . $code);
    $srcUnits = fn () => array_column($as3('return array_map(fn ($s) => array_diff_key($s, ["pair" => 1]), rspSources());'), 'units', 'id');
    same('restore partner: sent only appdata, nothing known of the partner yet — appdata only', [$id => ['share:appdata']], $srcUnits());
    partnerWritePrivate("$A3[data]/partner/state.json", ['pairs' => [$id => ['status' => ['agreed' => ['share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']]]]]);
    same('restore partner: a unit in agreed but not sent (settings.ini) is offered (sent ones first)', [$id => ['share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']], $srcUnits());
    $as3('rspLookJob([]); return true;');
    $plan3 = $as3('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $stamp . '"]);');
    same('restore partner: … the look asked for it, the tile and the plan have it', [['uso-backup-20261007-0200'], 'vm:Debian_VM', null, []],
        [array_column(($as3('return rspHeld("' . $id . '");')['units']['vm:Debian_VM'] ?? []), 'name'),
         $as3('return rspState();')[0]['units'][array_search('vm:Debian_VM', array_column($as3('return rspState();')[0]['units'] ?? [], 'unit'), true)]['unit'] ?? null,
         $plan3['problem'] ?? null, $plan3['blockers'] ?? null]);
    partnerWritePrivate("$A3[data]/partner/state.json", ['pairs' => [$id => ['status' => ['agreed' => null]]]]);
    same('restore partner: what the partner\'s list found wins — no agreed known (an office before 2.29), the unit it lists still offered', [$id => ['share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']], $srcUnits());
    partnerWritePrivate("$A3[data]/partner/state.json", ['pairs' => [$id => ['status' => ['agreed' => ['share:appdata', '../etc', 'place']]]]]);
    same('restore partner: an agreed list out of shape counts for nothing', [$id => ['share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']], $srcUnits());
    same('restore partner: rspPairUnits — send, agreed, what the list found (with moments), each once, never an odd name',
        ['share:a', 'vm:b', 'place', 'share:c'],
        rspPairUnits(['share:a', 'vm:b'], ['vm:b', 'place'], ['units' => ['share:c' => [['name' => 'x']], 'share:empty' => [], '../x' => [['name' => 'x']], 'share:a' => [['name' => 'y']]]]));

    $en = json_decode((string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_WEB . '/desks/restore/lang/en.json'), true);
    check('restore partner: «the package isn\'t at the partner — only the disks come back»', str_contains((string) ($en['note.partner_no_package'] ?? ''), "The package isn't at {name} — only the disks come back"));

    // ---- the pull: ssh | pv | mbuffer | zfs recv -s -u into the new dataset, then mounted
    partnerTestCalls($A['bin']);
    $run = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $stamp . '"]);'
        . ' $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); $code = rsJob([$jid]); return ["id" => $jid, "code" => $code, "j" => rsJournal($jid)];');
    $j = $run['j'] ?? [];
    $ds = "tank/appdata.restored-$stamp";
    same('restore partner: the pull went through', [0, 'ok', ['ok', 'ok']], [$run['code'] ?? null, $j['result'] ?? null, array_column($j['steps'] ?? [], 'state')], );
    $calls = partnerTestCalls($A['bin']);
    $zc = fn (string $verb) => array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && ($c[1] ?? '') === $verb));
    same('restore partner: zfs recv -s -u — legacy, noauto, not shared, never -F, into the new dataset', [['zfs', 'recv', '-s', '-u', '-o', 'mountpoint=legacy', '-o', 'canmount=noauto',
        '-x', 'sharesmb', '-x', 'sharenfs', "$ds@uso-backup-20261007-0200"]], $zc('recv'));
    $pipe = array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => in_array($c[0], ['pv', 'mbuffer'], true)));
    usort($pipe, fn ($a, $b) => strcmp($a[0], $b[0]));
    same('restore partner: … through pv and mbuffer', [['mbuffer', '-q', '-s', '128k', '-m', '256M'], ['pv', '-n', '-b', '-i', '2']], $pipe);
    same('restore partner: … the door asked for send-back with the pair\'s key', ['send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261007-0200', "$A[flash]/$id.key"],
        [array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'ssh'))[0][count(array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'ssh'))[0]) - 1] ?? null,
         array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'ssh'))[0][2] ?? null]);
    same('restore partner: … the properties kept, then mounted read-only', [[['zfs', 'set', 'canmount=noauto', $ds], ['zfs', 'set', 'mountpoint=legacy', $ds]],
        [['mount', '-t', 'zfs', '-o', 'ro,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec', $ds, "$tmp/A/restored/homeserver-share-appdata-$stamp"]]],
        [$zc('set'), array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'mount'))]);
    check('restore partner: the original untouched — nothing renamed, destroyed, set or received into it', !array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs'
        && (in_array($c[1] ?? '', ['rename', 'destroy'], true) || (in_array($c[1] ?? '', ['recv', 'set', 'create'], true) && (in_array('tank/appdata', $c, true) || in_array('tank/appdata@uso-backup-20261007-0200', $c, true))))));
    same('restore partner: the stream that came is B\'s copy of that moment', strlen("SNAP:uso-backup-20261007-0200 whole\n"), $zfsA()['snaps']["$ds@uso-backup-20261007-0200"]['used'] ?? null);
    same('restore partner: the journal records the pull (its guid) and its undo', [[$ds], [[['do' => 'drop', 'dataset' => $ds, 'path' => "$tmp/A/restored/homeserver-share-appdata-$stamp",
        'guid' => (string) abs(crc32($ds))]]]], [array_column($j['pulled'] ?? [], 'dataset'), [$j['steps'][0]['undo'] ?? null]]);
    check('restore partner: progress in the job file (pv\'s bytes)', ($j['steps'][0]['progress']['done'] ?? 0) > 0);
    check('restore partner: B\'s door logged it', str_contains((string) @file_get_contents("$B[data]/partner/door.log"), 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261007-0200 (whole)'));
    check('restore partner: the lock as holder restore, released', !is_file("$A[data]/unraid-backup/state/lock-holder.json"));
    // the pull as a moment of his files restores, and the same plan again — refused: never over
    $mnt = "$tmp/A/restored/homeserver-share-appdata-$stamp";
    @mkdir("$mnt/nextcloud", 0755, true);
    $m = $as('return rspRestored("/mnt/user/appdata/nextcloud");');
    same('restore partner: a moment «at <partner>» for a folder in the share', [["partner:{$run['id']}:share:appdata", "$mnt/nextcloud", 'homeserver', true, 1791336000]],
        array_map(fn ($x) => [$x['id'], $x['path'], $x['partner'], $x['kopia'], $x['time']], $m));
    same('restore partner: … none for another share', [], $as('return rspRestored("/mnt/user/media/x");'));
    same('restore partner: the same moment again into the same name — blocked, never over', 'restore_exists',
        $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $stamp . '"]);')['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null);

    // ---- «Remove what was pulled…»: exactly that dataset (name, guid, no children), unmounted first
    same('restore partner: the drop refuses anything not his', 'drop_refused', $as('$j = ["id" => "x"]; return rsDoDrop($j, ["dataset" => "tank/appdata"])["note"];'));
    same('restore partner: … another guid — refused', 'drop_other', $as('$j = ["id" => "x"]; return rsDoDrop($j, ["dataset" => "' . $ds . '", "guid" => "1"])["note"];'));
    $pb = $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "putback", "id" => "' . $run['id'] . '"]);');
    same('restore partner: its put back — only the drop, said in the preview', [['drop'], [['what' => 'drop', 'from' => $ds, 'to' => '']], []],
        [array_column($pb['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), $pb['aside'] ?? null, $pb['blockers'] ?? null]);
    partnerTestCalls($A['bin']);
    $undo = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "putback", "id" => "' . $run['id'] . '"]); $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); return [rsJob([$jid]), rsJournal($jid)["result"], rsJournal("' . $run['id'] . '")["putback"]["result"] ?? null];');
    $calls = partnerTestCalls($A['bin']);
    same('restore partner: dropped — unmounted, then zfs destroy -r of exactly it', [[0, 'ok', 'ok'], [['umount', $mnt]], [['zfs', 'destroy', '-r', $ds]]],
        [$undo, array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'umount')), array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && ($c[1] ?? '') === 'destroy'))]);
    check('restore partner: … the original and its snapshots still there', isset($zfsA()['ds']['tank/appdata']) && !isset($zfsA()['ds'][$ds]));
    same('restore partner: … no moment of it any more', [], $as('return rspRestored("/mnt/user/appdata/nextcloud");'));

    // ---- an interrupted pull keeps its token here; the next plan of the same moment goes on with send-back -t
    $zb = json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json"), true);
    $zb['send_interrupt'] = true;
    $zb['tokens']['1-abcdef0123-c8-789c0123456789'] = 'vault/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id/share-appdata@uso-backup-20261006-0200";
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json", json_encode($zb));
    $s2 = $at(6000);
    $first = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261006-0200", "stamp" => "' . $s2 . '"]);'
        . ' $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); rsJob([$jid]); return rsJournal($jid);');
    same('restore partner: interrupted — failed, resumable, the undo recorded anyway', ['failed', 'pull_failed', 'yes', 'drop'],
        [$first['result'] ?? null, $first['steps'][0]['note'] ?? null, $first['steps'][0]['params']['resumable'] ?? null, $first['steps'][0]['undo'][0]['do'] ?? null]);
    $zb['send_interrupt'] = false;
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json", json_encode($zb));
    $again = $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261006-0200", "stamp" => "' . $at(5000) . '"]);');
    same('restore partner: the next plan goes on in the same dataset', [true, "tank/appdata.restored-$s2", true],
        [$again['steps'][0]['resume'] ?? null, $again['steps'][0]['dataset'] ?? null, in_array('note.partner_resume', array_column($again['notes'] ?? [], 'key'), true)]);
    partnerTestCalls($A['bin']);
    $res = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261006-0200", "stamp" => "' . $at(5000) . '"]);'
        . ' $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); rsJob([$jid]); return rsJournal($jid)["result"];');
    $calls = partnerTestCalls($A['bin']);
    $sshc = array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'ssh'))[0] ?? [];
    same('restore partner: resumed — send-back -t with the token kept here, zfs recv -s -u into it (no -o)', ['ok', 'send-back share:appdata -t 1-abcdef0123-c8-789c0123456789',
        [['zfs', 'recv', '-s', '-u', "tank/appdata.restored-$s2"]]], [$res, end($sshc), array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && ($c[1] ?? '') === 'recv'))]);
    check('restore partner: … B sent the resumed stream (zfs send -t)', str_contains((string) @file_get_contents("$B[data]/partner/door.log"), 'send-back share:appdata uso-backup-20261006-0200 (resumed)'));

    // ---- the door refuses: said in the journal
    $zb['snaps'] = array_diff_key($zb['snaps'], ['vault/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id/vm-Debian_VM@uso-backup-20261007-0200" => 1]);
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json", json_encode($zb));
    $ref = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $at(4000) . '"]);'
        . ' $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); rsJob([$jid]); return rsJournal($jid);');
    same('restore partner: the door refuses (the moment is gone there) — said, nothing more done', ['failed', 'pull_refused_door', 'no_snapshot', ['failed', 'skipped', 'skipped', 'skipped']],
        [$ref['result'] ?? null, $ref['steps'][0]['note'] ?? null, $ref['steps'][0]['params']['why'] ?? null, array_column($ref['steps'] ?? [], 'state')]);

    // ---- the array stop ends the pull (rsWatch every 2 s; the pipe's processes terminated)
    $zb['send_sleep'] = 4;
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json", json_encode($zb));
    file_put_contents("$A[root]/var.ini", "fsState=\"Stopping\"\n");
    $t0 = microtime(true);
    $stop = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "partner", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $at(3000) . '"]);'
        . ' $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); rsJob([$jid]); return rsJournal($jid);');
    same('restore partner: the array stopping — the pull ends at once, never failed silently', ['failed', 'restore_array_stopping', 'pull_stopped'],
        [$stop['result'] ?? null, $stop['reason'] ?? null, $stop['steps'][0]['note'] ?? null]);
    check('restore partner: … within seconds, not after the stream', microtime(true) - $t0 < 4, (string) round(microtime(true) - $t0, 1));
    file_put_contents("$A[root]/var.ini", "fsState=\"Started\"\n");
    $sh = (string) file_get_contents(OFFICE_DIR . '/plugin/scripts/agent.sh');
    check('restore partner: agent.sh unmounts the pulls at the array stop (after drill_release ended the job)', (bool) preg_match('/drill_release.*\n(?:.*\n){0,3}\s*restored_release\s/', $sh)
        && str_contains($sh, 'RESTORED_ROOT="${USO_RESTORED_ROOT:-/mnt/addons/UnraidSecretaryOffice/restored}"') && str_contains($sh, 'local root=$RESTORED_ROOT ')
        && RSP_MOUNT_ROOT === '/mnt/addons/UnraidSecretaryOffice/restored');
    // never the live folder: a root of the test's own (USO_RESTORED_ROOT) — a real pull or an earlier test's mount there is none of this test's business
    $release = fn (string $root) => trim((string) shell_exec('USO_RESTORED_ROOT=' . escapeshellarg($root) . ' bash -c ' . escapeshellarg('source '
        . escapeshellarg(OFFICE_DIR . '/plugin/scripts/agent.sh') . '; LOG=' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/agent.log") . '; restored_release; echo "rc=$?"') . ' 2>&1'));
    @mkdir("$tmp/restored-root", 0755, true);
    same('restore partner: nothing mounted there — nothing done, nothing said', ['rc=0', false], [$release("$tmp/restored-root"), is_file("$tmp/agent.log")]);
    same('restore partner: an odd root (relative, «/», with a space) — nothing looked at', ['rc=0', 'rc=0', 'rc=0', false],
        [$release('restored'), $release('/'), $release("$tmp/restored root"), is_file("$tmp/agent.log")]);
    if (getenv('OFFICE_TESTS_GUARD') !== false) {       // the tests' own mount namespace (root): bind mounts nobody else sees
        @mkdir("$tmp/restored-src", 0755, true);
        @mkdir("$tmp/restored-root/appdata", 0755, true);
        @mkdir("$tmp/restored-other", 0755, true);
        exec('mount --bind ' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/restored-src") . ' ' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/restored-root/appdata") . ' && mount --bind '
            . escapeshellarg("$tmp/restored-src") . ' ' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/restored-other") . ' 2>&1', $o, $mc);
        $mounted = fn (string $at) => str_contains((string) file_get_contents('/proc/mounts'), " $at ");
        if ($mc === 0 && $mounted("$tmp/restored-root/appdata")) {
            $out = $release("$tmp/restored-root");
            same('restore partner: a pull mounted there — unmounted, its folder gone, said once; a mount elsewhere untouched',
                ['rc=0', false, false, true, true],
                [$out, $mounted("$tmp/restored-root/appdata"), is_dir("$tmp/restored-root/appdata"), $mounted("$tmp/restored-other"),
                 str_contains((string) @file_get_contents("$tmp/agent.log"), "1 of Mr. Restori's pulls unmounted ($tmp/restored-root)")]);
        } else {
            check('restore partner: a bind mount of the test\'s own for restored_release', false, implode(' ', $o));
        }
        exec('umount ' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/restored-other") . ' 2>/dev/null; umount ' . escapeshellarg("$tmp/restored-root/appdata") . ' 2>/dev/null');
    }
    sleep(4);           // the door's orphaned send (4 s) lets go of the pair's lock
    hardeningRm($tmp);
}

/**
 * Mr. Restori on the receiver: «Kept for <partner>» from received.json and the datasets here; «Start here…» (kind
 * partner_start) — the preflight (target, conflicts, refusals), the independent copy (zfs send | recv, never a clone,
 * the partner's dataset untouched), the files into their place, the VM defined from the copy's .uso-backup, an app's
 * template to the flash, an older copy without .uso-backup, the put back
 */
function testPartnerStart(): void
{
    if (posix_geteuid() !== 0) {
        check('partner start: root only — not run here', true);
        return;
    }
    $tmp = hardeningTmp('partner-start');
    exec('rm -rf ' . escapeshellarg($tmp) . '/*');
    [, $B, $id] = restorePartnerTestPair($tmp);
    $pd = 'vault/' . PARTNER_PARENT . "/$id";
    $user = "$tmp/B/user";
    $lv = "$tmp/B/libvirt";
    $tpl = "$tmp/B/templates";
    foreach (["$tmp/B/restored", "$user/domains", "$user/appdata", "$lv/qemu/nvram", "$lv/qemu/swtpm/tpm-states", $tpl] as $d) {
        @mkdir($d, 0755, true);
    }
    file_put_contents("$B[bin]/virsh", "#!/bin/bash\nprintf '%s\\n' \"\$*\" >>\"\$(dirname \"\$0\")/virsh.log\"\n[[ \"\$1\" == list ]] && printf ' Id   Name   State\\n----\\n -    Other  shut off\\n'\nexit 0\n");
    chmod("$B[bin]/virsh", 0755);
    $pre = 'date_default_timezone_set("UTC"); $GLOBALS["rs"]["restored_root"] = ' . var_export("$tmp/B/restored", true) . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["mounts_file"] = ' . var_export("$B[bin]/mounts", true)
        . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["var_ini"] = ' . var_export("$B[root]/var.ini", true) . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["user_root"] = ' . var_export($user, true) . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["libvirt"] = ' . var_export($lv, true)
        . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["templates"] = ' . var_export($tpl, true) . '; $GLOBALS["rs"]["shares_ini"] = ["appdata" => [], "domains" => [], "UnraidSecretaryOffice" => []]; $GLOBALS["rs"]["vm_states"] = ["Other" => "shut off"];';
    $as = fn (string $code) => partnerTestAs($B, $pre . $code);
    $zfsB = fn () => json_decode((string) file_get_contents("$B[bin]/zfs.json"), true);
    $at = fn (int $ago) => gmdate('Ymd-His', time() - $ago);
    $virsh = fn () => array_values(array_filter(explode("\n", (string) @file_get_contents("$B[bin]/virsh.log"))));
    $uuid = '12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789abc';
    // the copy's content as the mount would show it (the stand-in mount only notes the mount: the folder is filled here)
    $fixture = function (string $mnt, string $kind) use ($uuid): void {
        @mkdir("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/nvram', 0755, true);
        if ($kind === 'vm') {
            file_put_contents("$mnt/vdisk1.img", str_repeat('v', 4096));
            @mkdir("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . "/tpm/$uuid/tpm2", 0755, true);
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . "/tpm/$uuid/tpm2/tpm2-00.permall", 'tpm');
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . "/nvram/{$uuid}_VARS-pure-efi-tpm.fd", 'vars');
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/Debian_VM.xml', "<domain><name>Debian_VM</name><uuid>$uuid</uuid><devices><disk type='file'><source file='/mnt/user/domains/Debian_VM/vdisk1.img'/></disk>"
                . "<disk type='file' device='cdrom'><source file='/mnt/user/isos/debian.iso'/></disk><tpm model='tpm-tis'/></devices></domain>");
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/manifest.json', json_encode(['interface' => 1, 'engine' => '2.43', 'kind' => 'vm', 'name' => 'Debian_VM', 'folder' => 'Debian_VM', 'run' => '20261007-0200',
                'xml' => 'Debian_VM.xml', 'uuid' => $uuid, 'autostart' => false, 'disks' => [['target' => 'vda', 'source' => '/mnt/user/domains/Debian_VM/vdisk1.img']],
                'files' => [['path' => 'Debian_VM.xml', 'what' => 'xml'], ['path' => "nvram/{$uuid}_VARS-pure-efi-tpm.fd", 'what' => 'nvram'], ['path' => "tpm/$uuid/tpm2/tpm2-00.permall", 'what' => 'tpm']]]));
        } elseif ($kind === 'app') {
            @mkdir("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/db', 0755, true);
            @mkdir("$mnt/nextcloud", 0755, true);
            file_put_contents("$mnt/nextcloud/config.php", 'x');
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/my-nextcloud.xml', '<Container><Name>nextcloud</Name></Container>');
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/db/mariadb_nextcloud-db_nextcloud.sql.gz', 'dump');
            file_put_contents("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/manifest.json', json_encode(['interface' => 1, 'engine' => '2.43', 'kind' => 'app', 'name' => 'nextcloud', 'type' => 'template', 'containers' => [], 'files' => []]));
        } else {
            @rmdir("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/nvram');
            @rmdir("$mnt/" . RSP_INSIDE);
            file_put_contents("$mnt/vdisk1.img", 'old');
        }
    };

    // ---- the tile: what this office keeps of the partner, from received.json and the datasets here
    $kept = $as('return rspKept();');
    same('partner start: «Kept for <partner>» — the pair I receive from, its pool, the units the door noted (the place first)', [[$id, 'homeserver', 'vault', false, ['place', 'share:appdata', 'vm:Debian_VM']]],
        array_map(fn ($k) => [$k['id'], $k['name'], $k['pool'], $k['asleep'], array_column($k['units'], 'unit')], $kept));
    same('partner start: … per unit the moments on its dataset here, newest first, with sizes', [["$pd/share-appdata", 2, 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 1791336000, 10], ["$pd/vm-Debian_VM", 1, 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 1791336001, 10]],
        array_map(fn ($u) => [$u['dataset'], $u['n'], $u['snaps'][0]['name'] ?? null, $u['newest'], $u['snaps'][0]['referenced'] ?? null], array_slice($kept[0]['units'], 1)));
    check('partner start: nothing of a key in it', !str_contains(json_encode($kept), 'ssh-ed25519') && !str_contains(json_encode($kept), 'SHA256:'));
    same('partner start: the state carries it', ['vault'], array_column($as('return rsScan()["kept"];'), 'pool'));

    // ---- the preflight of a VM: the copy on the same pool, mounted; the files into domains/<vm>; the definition from .uso-backup
    $stamp = $at(7200);
    $plan = fn (array $r) => $as('return rsPlan(' . var_export($r + ['kind' => 'partner_start', 'pair' => $id, 'stamp' => $stamp], true) . ');');
    $p = $plan(['unit' => 'vm:Debian_VM', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200']);
    $ds = 'vault/' . RSP_PARENT . "/vm-Debian_VM.from-homeserver-$stamp";
    $mnt = "$tmp/B/restored/homeserver-vm-Debian_VM-$stamp";
    same('partner start: a VM — copy, mount, the files into domains/<vm>, then start_from; nothing blocks', [['pull_local', 'mount', 'copy', 'start_from'], "$pd/vm-Debian_VM@uso-backup-20261007-0200", $ds, $mnt, "$user/domains/Debian_VM", true, []],
        [array_column($p['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), $p['steps'][0]['source'] ?? null, $p['steps'][0]['dataset'] ?? null, $p['steps'][1]['path'] ?? null, $p['steps'][2]['to'] ?? null, $p['steps'][3]['define'] ?? null, $p['blockers'] ?? null], json_encode($p));
    same('partner start: … the dialog knows the target, the size twice (the copy and the files), the pool\'s room, what comes after', ['vm', 'Debian_VM', 20, true, 'after.partner_start_vm', 'note.partner_start_copy'],
        [$p['options']['kind'] ?? null, $p['target']['vm'] ?? null, $p['sizes']['need'] ?? null, ($p['sizes']['free'] ?? 0) > 0, $p['after'][0]['key'] ?? null, $p['notes'][0]['key'] ?? null]);
    same('partner start: … no domains share here — blocked, the share is the user\'s to make', 'restore_partner_share_needed',
        $as('$GLOBALS["rs"]["shares_ini"] = ["appdata" => []]; return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner_start", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null);
    same('partner start: … a VM of that name here — the definition refused in the preflight, the disks still come', [false, 'start_vm_exists', 'note.partner_start_vm_exists', 'after.partner_start_vm_by_hand'],
        (function () use ($as, $id) {
            $x = $as('$GLOBALS["rs"]["vm_states"] = ["Debian_VM" => "shut off"]; return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner_start", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);');
            return [$x['steps'][3]['define'] ?? null, $x['steps'][3]['define_why'] ?? null, $x['notes'][1]['key'] ?? null, $x['after'][0]['key'] ?? null];
        })());
    same('partner start: … the VM service off — said, the disks come', 'note.partner_start_vm_service_off',
        $as('$GLOBALS["rs"]["vm_states"] = null; return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner_start", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['notes'][1]['key'] ?? null);
    same('partner start: a moment the dataset doesn\'t hold — blocked', 'restore_partner_no_snap', $plan(['unit' => 'vm:Debian_VM', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261009-0200'])['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null);
    same('partner start: a unit not kept here, a path, an unknown pair — unknown', ['unknown_target', 'unknown_target', 'unknown_target'],
        [$plan(['unit' => 'share:media', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200'])['problem'] ?? null, $plan(['unit' => '../etc', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200'])['problem'] ?? null,
         $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner_start", "pair" => "deadbeef", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['problem'] ?? null]);

    // ---- the job: zfs send | recv on the same pool (never a clone, the partner's dataset untouched), rsync into the folder, the definition
    $fixture($mnt, 'vm');
    partnerTestCalls($B['bin']);
    @unlink("$B[bin]/virsh.log");
    $run = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "partner_start", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "vm:Debian_VM", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200", "stamp" => "' . $stamp . '"]);'
        . ' $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); $code = rsJob([$jid]); return ["id" => $jid, "code" => $code, "j" => rsJournal($jid)];');
    $j = $run['j'] ?? [];
    same('partner start: the job went through — the copy, the mount, the files, the definition', [0, 'ok', ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']], [$run['code'] ?? null, $j['result'] ?? null, array_column($j['steps'] ?? [], 'state')], json_encode($j));
    $calls = partnerTestCalls($B['bin']);
    $zc = fn (string $verb) => array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && ($c[1] ?? '') === $verb));
    same('partner start: zfs send -L -c of the partner\'s moment | zfs recv -u into the restored area — legacy, noauto, not shared, no clone, never -F',
        [[['zfs', 'send', '-L', '-c', "$pd/vm-Debian_VM@uso-backup-20261007-0200"]], [['zfs', 'recv', '-u', '-o', 'mountpoint=legacy', '-o', 'canmount=noauto', '-x', 'sharesmb', '-x', 'sharenfs', "$ds@uso-backup-20261007-0200"]], []],
        [$zc('send'), $zc('recv'), $zc('clone')]);
    check('partner start: the partner\'s dataset and its snapshots exactly as they were — nothing renamed, destroyed, set or received into it',
        !array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && in_array($c[1] ?? '', ['rename', 'destroy', 'clone', 'promote'], true))
        && !array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && in_array($c[1] ?? '', ['set', 'recv', 'create'], true) && array_filter($c, fn ($a) => str_starts_with((string) $a, "$pd/")))
        && isset($zfsB()['snaps']["$pd/vm-Debian_VM@uso-backup-20261007-0200"]), json_encode($calls));
    check('partner start: … nothing through the door, nothing to the sender', !array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'ssh'));
    same('partner start: the copy is a dataset of this office, mounted read-only, recorded as pulled (a moment for his files restores, mounted again at the agent\'s start)',
        [true, [['mount', '-t', 'zfs', '-o', 'ro,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec', $ds, $mnt]], [$ds], true, "$user/domains/Debian_VM"],
        [isset($zfsB()['ds'][$ds]), array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'mount')), array_column($j['pulled'] ?? [], 'dataset'), $j['pulled'][0]['local'] ?? null, $j['pulled'][0]['path'] ?? null]);
    same('partner start: … rspPulled() lists it like a pull', [$ds], array_column(array_filter($as('return rspPulled();'), fn ($x) => $x['journal'] === $run['id']), 'dataset'));
    same('partner start: the files are in domains/<vm> — the disk and the copy\'s .uso-backup', [true, true], [is_file("$user/domains/Debian_VM/vdisk1.img"), is_file("$user/domains/Debian_VM/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/manifest.json')]);
    $xml = (string) @file_get_contents($B["data"] . "/restore/{$run['id']}/start-3-Debian_VM.xml");
    // 1.60.1: from another server (the manifest names no host of this one) - fitted: the ISO that isn't here emptied, its drive kept
    same('partner start: the VM defined from the copy\'s XML with its disk path pointed at the new folder (the ISO not here: its drive kept, empty)', [true, true, true],
        [str_contains($xml, "<source file=\"$user/domains/Debian_VM/vdisk1.img\"/>") || str_contains($xml, "<source file='$user/domains/Debian_VM/vdisk1.img'/>"),
         !str_contains($xml, 'debian.iso') && str_contains($xml, 'device="cdrom"'), (bool) preg_grep('/^define .*start-3-Debian_VM\.xml$/', $virsh())], $xml . json_encode($virsh()));
    same('partner start: … UEFI variables and TPM state put in place (nothing was there), said in the step', [true, true, 'start_vm', 1, 1, 'put'],
        [is_file("$lv/qemu/nvram/{$uuid}_VARS-pure-efi-tpm.fd"), is_file("$lv/qemu/swtpm/tpm-states/$uuid/tpm2/tpm2-00.permall"), $j['steps'][3]['note'] ?? null,
         $j['steps'][3]['params']['rewritten'] ?? null, $j['steps'][3]['params']['nvram'] ?? null, $j['steps'][3]['params']['tpm'] ?? null]);
    same('partner start 1.60.1: … the fitting said in the step, the original XML kept beside the package', [['cdrom'], true],
        [array_column($j['steps'][3]['params']['adapted'] ?? [], 'code'), is_file("$user/domains/Debian_VM/" . RSP_INSIDE . '/Debian_VM.xml.original')]);
    same('partner start: the undo recorded — the definition, the files put, the folder, the copy', [['undefine', 'aside', 'aside'], ['aside'], ['drop']],
        [array_column($j['steps'][3]['undo'] ?? [], 'do'), array_column($j['steps'][2]['undo'] ?? [], 'do'), array_column($j['steps'][0]['undo'] ?? [], 'do')]);
    check('partner start: the lock released', !is_file("$B[data]/unraid-backup/state/lock-holder.json"));

    // ---- the same VM again: the folder is taken — the preflight says so and offers beside; a VM of that name is here now
    $p2 = $plan(['unit' => 'vm:Debian_VM', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'stamp' => $at(6000)]);
    same('partner start: the folder holds data — blocked with the two choices (cancel, beside as <vm>.from-<partner>)', ['restore_partner_start_exists', "$user/domains/Debian_VM", "$user/domains/Debian_VM.from-homeserver"],
        [$p2['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null, $p2['options']['conflict']['path'] ?? null, $p2['options']['conflict']['beside_as'] ?? null]);
    $p3 = $plan(['unit' => 'vm:Debian_VM', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'stamp' => $at(6000), 'beside' => true]);
    same('partner start: … beside: the files go to <vm>.from-<partner>, nothing blocks, said', [[], "$user/domains/Debian_VM.from-homeserver", 'note.partner_start_beside'],
        [$p3['blockers'] ?? null, $p3['steps'][2]['to'] ?? null, $p3['notes'][1]['key'] ?? null]);

    // ---- «Put back»: the definition removed, the files put aside (never deleted), the copy destroyed — the partner's dataset stays
    $pb = $as('return rsPlan(["kind" => "putback", "id" => "' . $run['id'] . '"]);');
    same('partner start: the put back — undefine, the nvram and TPM aside, the folder aside, the copy dropped; the VM must be shut off', [['undefine', 'aside', 'aside', 'aside', 'drop'], []],
        [array_column($pb['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), $pb['blockers'] ?? null], json_encode($pb));
    partnerTestCalls($B['bin']);
    @unlink("$B[bin]/virsh.log");
    $undo = $as('$p = rsPlan(["kind" => "putback", "id" => "' . $run['id'] . '"]); $jid = rsLaunch($p, false); return [rsJob([$jid]), rsJournal($jid)["result"], rsJournal("' . $run['id'] . '")["putback"]["result"] ?? null];');
    $calls = partnerTestCalls($B['bin']);
    same('partner start: … done: undefined (nvram and TPM kept for the aside), the folder aside, exactly the copy destroyed', [[0, 'ok', 'ok'], true, [['zfs', 'destroy', '-r', $ds]], false, true],
        [$undo, (bool) preg_grep('/^undefine Debian_VM --keep-nvram --keep-tpm$/', $virsh()), array_values(array_filter($calls, fn ($c) => $c[0] === 'zfs' && ($c[1] ?? '') === 'destroy')),
         is_dir("$user/domains/Debian_VM"), count(glob("$user/domains/Debian_VM.putback-*") ?: []) === 1], json_encode($calls));
    check('partner start: … the partner\'s dataset and its moment still there, the copy gone', isset($zfsB()['ds']["$pd/vm-Debian_VM"]) && isset($zfsB()['snaps']["$pd/vm-Debian_VM@uso-backup-20261007-0200"]) && !isset($zfsB()['ds'][$ds]));

    // ---- a share: the user makes it first; empty = filled; with data = only the copy, then «Restore…» per folder
    $s1 = $plan(['unit' => 'share:appdata', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'stamp' => $at(5000)]);
    same('partner start: a share that is here and empty — copy, mount, the files into it, start_from (an app\'s package?)', [['pull_local', 'mount', 'copy', 'start_from'], "$user/appdata", true, 'after.partner_start_share'],
        [array_column($s1['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), $s1['steps'][2]['to'] ?? null, $s1['steps'][2]['into_empty'] ?? null, $s1['after'][0]['key'] ?? null]);
    same('partner start: … the share missing — blocked, make it under Shares first', 'restore_partner_share_needed',
        $as('$GLOBALS["rs"]["shares_ini"] = ["domains" => []]; return rsPlan(["kind" => "partner_start", "pair" => "' . $id . '", "unit" => "share:appdata", "snap" => "uso-backup-20261007-0200"]);')['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null);
    file_put_contents("$user/appdata/keep.txt", 'mine');
    $s2 = $plan(['unit' => 'share:appdata', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'stamp' => $at(5000)]);
    $s3 = $plan(['unit' => 'share:appdata', 'snap' => 'uso-backup-20261007-0200', 'stamp' => $at(5000), 'beside' => true]);
    same('partner start: … the share holds data — blocked; with the choice only the copy comes (then «Restore…» per folder)', ['restore_partner_start_exists', 'share', ['pull_local', 'mount', 'start_from'], 'look', 'after.partner_start_copy_only'],
        [$s2['blockers'][0]['key'] ?? null, $s2['options']['conflict']['kind'] ?? null, array_column($s3['steps'] ?? [], 'do'), $s3['steps'][2]['kind'] ?? null, $s3['after'][0]['key'] ?? null]);
    unlink("$user/appdata/keep.txt");
    // the job: an app's package in the copy — the template to the flash, the dumps named; a second time the template is left as it is
    $st = $at(5000);
    $mnt2 = "$tmp/B/restored/homeserver-share-appdata-$st";
